{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "8f2c1d40-7b3e-4a56-9c81-shifteaze0001",
    "name": "ShiftEaze AI Calling",
    "description": "Five ShiftEaze calling scenarios in English, Hindi and Gujarati.\n\n## Order to work through this\n\n1. **0. Health** — confirm the server is up\n2. **1. Discovery** — see what scenarios exist\n3. **2. Preview** — proof-read the exact spoken lines BEFORE dialling anyone\n4. **3. Test without a phone** — hold a full conversation over HTTP (no Twilio, no tunnel)\n5. **4. Place a real call** — only once 2 and 3 look right\n6. **5. Outcomes** — read back what happened\n\n## Collection variables\n\nEdit these once under the collection's **Variables** tab and every request picks them up:\n\n| Variable | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| `base_url` | `http://127.0.0.1:8000` for local runs |\n| `to_phone_number` | Who to call, E.164 with country code |\n| `employee_name` | Operator's name as spoken |\n| `terminal` | e.g. `CT3` |\n| `supervisor_name` | Named in escalation replies |\n| `session_id` | Any string; groups a text-test conversation |\n| `call_sid` | Auto-filled after `POST /scenarios/call` |\n\n## Two rules for writing facts\n\nThese strings go straight into a text-to-speech engine.\n\n1. **Never send `14:00`** — send `दोपहर 2` / `બપોરે 2` / `2 in the afternoon`. TTS reads `14:00` as \"fourteen hundred\".\n2. **The Hindi/Gujarati scripts already contain बजे / વાગ્યે** — send `सुबह 8`, NOT `सुबह 8 बजे`, or the operator hears *\"8 baje baje\"*.\n\nUse **2. Preview** to catch exactly this.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "base_url", "value": "http://127.0.0.1:8000", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "to_phone_number", "value": "+91XXXXXXXXXX", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "employee_name", "value": "Amit", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "terminal", "value": "CT3", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "supervisor_name", "value": "Suresh", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "session_id", "value": "postman-test-1", "type": "string" },
    { "key": "call_sid", "value": "", "type": "string" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "0. Health",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Health check",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('server is up', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('reports healthy', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json().status).to.eql('healthy'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": [""] },
            "description": "Should return `{\"status\":\"healthy\"}`. If this fails, the server isn't running — see START_HERE.md."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "1. Discovery",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "List all scenarios",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('all five scenarios present', () => pm.expect(pm.response.json()).to.have.lengthOf(5));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": { "raw": "{{base_url}}/scenarios", "host": ["{{base_url}}"], "path": ["scenarios"] },
            "description": "All five scenarios with their ids, languages, branch keys and required facts."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Get one scenario (full knowledge base)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scenarios/shift_confirm",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["scenarios", "shift_confirm"]
            },
            "description": "Every script line in all three languages, the keyword hints, the outcome codes, and the `knowledge_base` guardrails the AI works from.\n\nSwap the path segment for: `punch_in_remind`, `absence_priority`, `ot_request`, `punch_out_remind`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Reload scenarios from disk",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scenarios/reload",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["scenarios", "reload"]
            },
            "description": "Re-reads `scenarios/*.json`. Edit a script line or keyword list, hit this, and the very next call uses it — no server restart.\n\nReturns `400` with the specific problem if a JSON is malformed, so a broken script can't half-load."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
