    {
      "name": "3. Test without a phone",
      "description": "Drives the identical flow engine over HTTP. No Twilio, no tunnel, no phone — costs only Claude tokens. This is where you verify behaviour.",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Turn 1 — Hindi, operator says नहीं",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('200 OK', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "pm.test('matched the no branch', () => pm.expect(b.matched_branch).to.eql('no'));",
                  "pm.test('call stays open to collect the reason', () => pm.expect(b.call_ended).to.be.false);",
                  "console.log('agent asks:', b.agent_reply);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } },
              "raw": "{\n  \"scenario_id\": \"shift_confirm\",\n  \"language\": \"hi\",\n  \"session_id\": \"{{session_id}}\",\n  \"facts\": {\n    \"employee_name\": \"{{employee_name}}\",\n    \"date\": \"2 अगस्त\",\n    \"time\": \"सुबह 8\",\n    \"shift_name\": \"Day\",\n    \"terminal\": \"{{terminal}}\",\n    \"supervisor_name\": \"{{supervisor_name}}\"\n  },\n  \"message\": \"नहीं\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scenarios/test-turn",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["scenarios", "test-turn"]
            },
            "description": "First call for a `session_id` also returns the `opening_line`.\n\nThe operator gave no reason, so the agent asks for one and the call stays open — run **Turn 2** next with the same `session_id`."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Turn 2 — same session, operator gives the reason",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('call closes', () => pm.expect(b.call_ended).to.be.true);",
                  "pm.test('outcome recorded', () => pm.expect(b.outcome).to.eql('absent_with_reason'));",
                  "pm.test('reason captured verbatim', () => pm.expect(b.collected.absence_reason).to.be.a('string').and.not.empty);",
                  "console.log('captured reason:', b.collected.absence_reason);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } },
              "raw": "{\n  \"scenario_id\": \"shift_confirm\",\n  \"language\": \"hi\",\n  \"session_id\": \"{{session_id}}\",\n  \"message\": \"मेरे पिताजी की तबीयत खराब है, हॉस्पिटल जाना है\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scenarios/test-turn",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["scenarios", "test-turn"]
            },
            "description": "Same `session_id` continues the conversation — `facts` can be omitted, the session remembers them.\n\nThe reason is captured **verbatim** and NOT re-classified as a new branch."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Negation trap — \"haan nahi aa paunga\"",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('opens with haan but classified as no', () => pm.expect(b.matched_branch).to.eql('no'));",
                  "pm.test('still asks WHY - the reason is compulsory', () => pm.expect(b.call_ended).to.be.false);",
                  "console.log('branch:', b.matched_branch, '| collected:', JSON.stringify(b.collected));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } },
              "raw": "{\n  \"scenario_id\": \"shift_confirm\",\n  \"language\": \"hi\",\n  \"session_id\": \"negation-trap\",\n  \"facts\": {\n    \"employee_name\": \"{{employee_name}}\",\n    \"date\": \"2 अगस्त\",\n    \"time\": \"सुबह 8\",\n    \"shift_name\": \"Day\",\n    \"terminal\": \"{{terminal}}\",\n    \"supervisor_name\": \"{{supervisor_name}}\"\n  },\n  \"message\": \"haan nahi aa paunga yaar, tabiyat kharab hai\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scenarios/test-turn",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["scenarios", "test-turn"]
            },
            "description": "**This is the request that shows why the AI matters.**\n\nThe utterance opens with *haan* (yes) but means no. A keyword-matching IVR records the exact opposite answer. The classifier gets it right. The reason is compulsory, so the agent still asks why even though one was volunteered in the same breath - send the reason as the next turn (same session_id) to close the call."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Simulate silence / no answer",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const b = pm.response.json();",
                  "pm.test('silence branch', () => pm.expect(b.matched_branch).to.eql('silence'));",
                  "pm.test('scenario-specific no-answer outcome', () => pm.expect(b.outcome).to.eql('no_response_treated_as_decline'));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "options": { "raw": { "language": "json" } },
              "raw": "{\n  \"scenario_id\": \"absence_priority\",\n  \"language\": \"hi\",\n  \"session_id\": \"silence-test\",\n  \"facts\": {\n    \"employee_name\": \"{{employee_name}}\",\n    \"date\": \"5 अगस्त\",\n    \"time\": \"रात 8\",\n    \"terminal\": \"{{terminal}}\",\n    \"supervisor_name\": \"{{supervisor_name}}\"\n  },\n  \"message\": \"\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{base_url}}/scenarios/test-turn",
              "host": ["{{base_url}}"],
              "path": ["scenarios", "test-turn"]
            },
            "description": "An empty `message` simulates a timeout / unintelligible audio.\n\nNote each scenario has its own no-answer consequence: Absence Prediction treats silence as a **decline** (replacement begins), whereas Shift Confirmation records `no_response` and notifies the supervisor."
          }
        },
